            "n_events": 40,
            "result_text": "I've created `/app/filter.py` that removes JavaScript and XSS vectors from HTML. The script:\n\n**Removes:**\n- `<script>` tags and all content within them\n- Event handler attributes (`onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, etc) with both quoted and unquoted values\n- `javascript:` protocol in href/src/action/formaction attributes\n\n**Preserves:**\n- All other HTML structure and content\n- Document formatting and whitespace\n- Safe attributes and elements (tables, headers, links with safe URLs, etc)\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython filter.py input.html\n```\n\nThe script modifies the file in-place. For example:\n- `<div onclick=\"alert('xss')\">content</div>` → `<div>content</div>`\n- `<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\">click</a>` → `<a>click</a>`\n- `<script>alert('xss')</script>` → removed entirely\n- `<table><tr><td>data</td></tr></table>` → preserved unchanged"
        }
